Package: scratch-link
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, bluez
Recommends: libayatana-appindicator3-1
Suggests: scratch
Description: local Bluetooth bridge between Scratch and peripherals
 Scratch Link runs a small WebSocket server that lets Scratch talk to
 Bluetooth LE and Bluetooth Classic (RFCOMM) devices such as micro:bit,
 LEGO BOOST and LEGO WeDo 2.0. It implements the Scratch Link network
 protocol and accesses BlueZ over D-Bus, so it needs no extra capabilities,
 certificates or hosts-file changes.
 .
 The package includes a GTK status window, a tray icon when AppIndicator is
 available, and a systemd user service for headless operation.
